approvedApplications.proposal:
Change of Use relating to all ground floor units from a mix of A1/A3/Sui Generis uses to a flexible use to include:
Class E (a) Retail other than for the sale of hot food, (b) the sale of food and drink which is mostly consumed on the premises, (d) Indoor sport, recreation or fitness;
Class F1 (b) For the display of artwork (not for sale or hire), (e) As a public hall or exhibition hall;
Class F2 (b) Community halls and meeting places; and
Sui Generis uses as a: theatre, amusement arcade, public house, wine bar or drinking establishment, drinking establishment with expanded food provision, and live music performance venue.

pendingApplications.proposal:
Demolition of the curtilage listed Gun Shop and Long Shed buildings and internal and external repairs and alterations to the Grade II* listed Whist House including:
• full roof and external tile hanging renewal;
• replacement of concrete floors and dilapidated timber floor areas at ground floor level with breathable limecrete, and the addition of a pamment floor and associated modifications to historic stair and panelling;
• removal of failing render and the repair/restoration of brickwork, plinths and quoins;
• repair and renewal of failed lath and plaster walls and ceilings;
• joinery repairs and modifications as scheduled including upgrading and replacement of doors and windows;
• alterations to internal openings, partitions and the addition of glazed screens;
• new tile hung and glazed lift addition to south elevation with 4 no. new associated new openings;
• demolitions of west garden walls;
• removal of modern external slabs and new brick plinths to existing columns where ground level reduced.

Redevelopment of the site for a mixed use development comprising:

•	Change of use, upward extension and external alterations to the Locomotive Shed building to provide 412 residential dwellings and commercial floorspace (577m2) (Use Class E);
•	Change of use, upward extension and external alterations to the Engine Shed building to provide 20 residential dwellings and commercial floorspace (724m2) (Use Class E);
•	Erection of four new buildings providing 383 residential dwellings, internal parking spaces and commercial floorspace (64m2) (Use Class E);
•	Change of use of the Paint Shop building to provide commercial floorspace (108m2) (Use Class E); and
•	Change of use of the Acetylene Store (55m2) and Clock Tower (70m2) buildings to provide commercial floorspace (Use Class E) and/or community floorspace (Use Class F2),

Plus associated infrastructure, landscaping, parking, servicing, access and other associated works.
